Birthdays are great,
As someone once said—
They remind you who's living,
And who’s long since dead.

Strangers wish brightly,
Like the warmth of the sun,
With vibrant hues of morning—
Yes, birthdays are fun.

Go make your wishes,
Blow candles one by one,
While laughter surrounds you—
Oh, birthdays are fun.

Long-lost friends
Connect one by one—
Oh really, birthdays are fun.

The people who swore
They’d never see your face,
Or claimed they'd vanish
Without a trace,
They still show up to say, “Hey—
Have a good one.”
Oh yes… birthdays are fun.

Forget the gifts,
The cards, the money—
Just hold space for me, please,
Don’t make it all sunny.
Don’t break my heart—
I’ll listen too, hun.
Birthdays aren’t forever…
Still, they'll be fun.

You won’t mind
If someone forgets your big day—
You just want them
To come back someday,
And say,
“Hey… belated happy birthday.”

Surrounded by blessings,
Memories, and loved ones—
Oh yes…
Birthdays are fun.
